<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  CBR005 Repairs Summary, ported from legacy's JasperServer report
  (cbr-legacy jasper-server .../CBR005_RepairSummary1_jrxml), its layout kept but for what it got
  wrong:
  - The structure header was three bands, one per mix of bridge-or-culvert and sort, and the fourth
    was missing: under the default sort, and under Road Name, a culvert's repairs printed with no
    header at all. One band now heads every structure.
  - Longitude and latitude printed as degrees, minutes and seconds under two sorts, rounding the
    degrees and minutes rather than truncating them (53.92 printed as 54), and as decimals under the
    third. Every sort now prints them as degrees, minutes and seconds, worked out correctly.
  - Nothing said which inspection a group of repairs came from: each group now opens with its
    inspection's date, or "Not attached to an inspection".
  - The PEng Comment, and the Inspection Comment of an inspection without one, printed as an empty
    labelled box; each prints only when there is a comment.
  - The "Repair Description" heading sat 56 points right of its column; it is over it now.
  - The report's header was a title, on the first page only, though each structure starts a page of
    its own; it is the page header now, on every page.

  As in the other reports, the port fills from rows rather than SQL - legacy called
  CBR_REPAIR_SUMMARY with a WHERE clause built as a string - every field already formatted as
  legacy's patterns printed it. The ministry line (the CBR_HEADER subreport) is P_MINISTRY, the
  logo comes from the classpath through P_LOGO, and Date Printed is P_DATE_PRINTED, in Pacific time.
-->
